This page is hand-written. It exists to fix the shape of a block before `garden.c` is
written, so the generator has an output to aim at rather than a guess to encode. Every
element below is one the generator must be able to emit.

> Marginalia. This is where the page argues with itself. It sits in the margin above
> 62rem and inline below it.

The header above carries the growth stage and the date. A block that hasn't been touched
in a long time says so. Nothing here pretends to be finished.

## a transcluded block

The construct below is a transclusion. The same file also lives at its own URL and inside
any number of collections. One file, three lives — this is the whole design.

![[some-quote]]

## a contradiction

Declared in the header as `contra`. Both blocks then appear paired on
[[contradictions]]. The edge is symmetric — declaring it once is enough.
